  "text": "The learning rate is non-monotonic in the transition probability. It rises rapidly as p_tr increases from 0, peaks, and then declines slowly, eventually reaching zero. When transitions are very rare, a low learning rate gives slow, stable convergence. At moderate rates, faster learning is needed to exploit the shorter stays in each environment. When transitions are too frequent, agents evolve little or no learning and stay near the mean of the two environments.",
