 "T_9.png": {
  "text": "NFPA and FPSA vastly outperform GMRES and DSA in nearly all cases, usually by orders of magnitude in both runtime and iteration count. For SRK and EK, NFPA and FPSA take about 0.3\u20131.4 s and 5\u201326 iterations. DSA needs thousands of seconds and tens of thousands of iterations, and GMRES needs roughly 50\u2013200 s. NFPA and FPSA are very similar to each other, with FPSA slightly faster per run because each iteration is cheaper. For HGK, NFPA and FPSA need more time and iterations as g increases, but they still beat GMRES and DSA. The one exception is at g = 0.9, where DSA's runtime is closer, though still much slower.",
