 "T_10.png": {
  "text": "It is the band-geometric origin of the effect. The intrinsic crossed nonlinear Hall conductivity is set by the momentum-space curl of the interlayer BCP over the occupied states, which makes it a Fermi-surface property. The interlayer BCP is the E\u22a5-space counterpart of the BCP and is nonzero only for layer-hybridized states. It is suppressed where a state is fully layer-polarized and is largest near band near-degeneracies with strong hybridization. Its curl is a time-reversal-even pseudoscalar, so it is allowed only in chiral structures such as twisted bilayers. It also flips sign when the twist direction is reversed.",
