 "T_16.png": {
  "text": "Superconducting proximity generally suppresses the Kondo effect, especially when the gap 2\u0394 exceeds T_K. However, in the sub-gap regime it can also enhance or induce Kondo screening. In this system, the non-local pairing produces CAR exchange, which can by itself cause a two-stage Kondo screening. This leaves a residual conductance at particle-hole symmetry. CAR exchange competes with ferromagnetic RKKY coupling. Coupling to the superconductor also shifts the first-stage Kondo temperature: it grows with \u0393_S1 as T\u0303_K = T_K\u00b7exp(\u03c0\u0393_S1\u00b2/(2\u0393U)).",
