 "T_30.png": {
  "text": "The paper proposes a probabilistic interpretation of the LMS filter. It uses a linear-Gaussian state-space model with a random-walk (diffusion) parameter. The exact Gaussian posterior, which gives RLS, is approximated by an isotropic Gaussian that minimizes the KL divergence. The mean is kept and the variance is set to Tr(\u03a3)/M. This yields a linear-complexity, adaptive step-size LMS algorithm. The step size is \u03b7_k = (\u03c3\u0302\u00b2_{k-1}+\u03c3_d\u00b2)/((\u03c3\u0302\u00b2_{k-1}+\u03c3_d\u00b2)\u2016x_k\u2016\u00b2+\u03c3_n\u00b2). The algorithm has only two parameters, \u03c3_d\u00b2 and \u03c3_n\u00b2, and also gives an estimate of the error variance.",
